on the one hand and the University on the other;
(m)
to delegate to the Vice-Chancellor or to any of the committees of the Academic Council, any of its powers;
(n)
to assess and make recommendations laying down standards of accommodation, equipment, library, maintenance and
other physical facilities required for each faculty; and
(o)
